@startuml frontend_product_boundary
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java dfb90cac4e233e09a0b8f047f7e9f4682f5ad238. Thinking-only evidence: 4cc8dd86 frontend/src/components/ThinkingDisclosure.vue template; target displays original model reasoning.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/App.vue submit; frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts sendMessage, dispatchSseFrame.
' Observed behavior: the internal workbench still consumes legacy Runtime request-scoped SSE and separate controls.
' Contract baseline: design 2ee2a3211da68ad87b0d9cab353e691b00bdaebd.
' Contract references: public-chat-alignment.md section 1, relative to this topic.
' Target-only architecture: product integration through Mate; no direct Runtime fallback.
' Design reason: public identity, protocol, and data visibility do not equal the internal transport.
title Product boundary - target-only integration
left to right direction
actor "User" as User
rectangle "Product browser" {
  component "Chat workspace\nno credential forms" as Workspace
  component "Public Chat Gateway" as Gateway
  component "Safe event reducer" as Reducer
}
rectangle "Host and Mate boundary" {
  component "Host identity transport\nintegration gate" as Host
  component "Public Chat API\nPOST JSON / GET live / GET history" as Mate
  component "Authorization and\nChat / Session mapping" as Mapping
  component "Safe event and\nhistory bridge - gate" as Bridge
}
rectangle "Internal Runtime - target contract" {
  component "Session API\nPOST SSE / GET numeric pages" as Runtime
}
User --> Workspace
Workspace --> Gateway
Gateway --> Host
Host --> Mate
Mate --> Mapping
Mapping --> Runtime
Runtime --> Bridge : committed events and preview
Bridge --> Mate : explicit public projection
Gateway --> Reducer : validated receipt, live, history
Reducer --> Workspace : immutable view
note bottom of Mate
Keep public and internal contracts separate.
Target correlation, tool result projection,
history snapshot bridging, and authentication
must be verified before production enablement.
end note
@enduml

